--- body ---
## Context

Figure 1 (`fig_census_direct.pdf`) currently colors each model with a
hash-derived hue (`_model_color` in `plot_method_convergence.py`). The
manuscript's Annex A groups the 16 journal-lineup models by language
family (EN: Anthropic + OpenAI, FR: Mistral, ZH: Alibaba + DeepSeek).
A family-coded palette would let readers see family-level patterns at a
glance. Beyond Figure 1, every plot in `src/aedist/plot_*.py` currently
chooses its own colors ad hoc, so the same model appears in different
hues across figures — visually incoherent and bug-prone when slides and
report sit side by side.

This ticket therefore introduces **one presentation-configuration file**
that defines a color per model family. All plot scripts must read from
it. No plot script may hardcode model or family colors.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/util.py` — already exports `COLOR_HALLUC`, `COLOR_REFERENCE`;
  natural home for `family_color(model: str) -> tuple`.
- `experiments/figures.toml` — already used by `plot_regimes_scatter.py`;
  good candidate location for the family palette under a new
  `[presentation.family_colors]` section.
- `src/aedist/models.py` — check whether `family` is already a registered
  field on model entries. If not, add it.
- All `src/aedist/plot_*.py`:
  - `plot_method_convergence.py` — `_model_color()` (line ~28)
  - `plot_ablation.py`, `plot_base_vs_census.py`, `plot_census.py`,
    `plot_pareto.py`, `plot_regimes_scatter.py`, `plot_scaling_curve.py`
  - Audit each for hardcoded model/family colors; route through the
    shared helper.

## Actions

1. **Confirm family metadata.** Locate where model family is recorded
   (model registry vs. inferred from lab/slug). If not present, add
   `family: "EN" | "FR" | "ZH"` to the journal-lineup models. The
   registry is the source of truth; never re-derive family inside plot
   scripts.
2. **Add the presentation config.** Append a `[presentation.family_colors]`
   table to `experiments/figures.toml` (or a new `presentation.toml` if
   `figures.toml` should stay strictly about layout). Define one
   colorblind-safe hue per family (Wong palette or ColorBrewer Set2).
   Include a `default` fallback hue for unknown families.
3. **Expose a single helper.** In `src/aedist/util.py`, add
   `family_color(model_or_family: str) -> tuple[float, float, float]`
   reading from the config. Cache the parsed config at module load.
4. **Refactor every plot script.** Remove any hardcoded model/family
   colors and route through `family_color()`. Drop the old hash-derived
   `_model_color()` from `plot_method_convergence.py`. For figures that
   need within-family lightness variation, derive it deterministically
   from the model slug, not from a hash.
5. **Legend discipline.** Each figure that uses family colors emits a
   small in-figure legend with the EN/FR/ZH mapping. Where space is
   constrained (slides), the slide-side caption or overlay can carry the
   legend instead.
6. **Rebuild artifacts.** Regenerate `slides/inputs/generated/fig_*.pdf`
   and `report/inputs/generated/fig_*.pdf` via the existing Makefile
   targets.

## Test

- `tests/test_family_colors.py` (new):
  - `family_color("claude-opus-4.6") == family_color("gpt-5.5")` (both EN)
  - `family_color("claude-opus-4.6") != family_color("mistral-large-2512")` (EN vs FR)
  - `family_color("mistral-large-2512") != family_color("deepseek-v4-pro")` (FR vs ZH)
  - `family_color("unknown-model")` returns the default fallback hue.
- `tests/test_no_hardcoded_plot_colors.py` (new, `@pytest.mark.adherence`):
  grep every `src/aedist/plot_*.py` for hex literals (`#[0-9A-Fa-f]{3,6}`)
  and RGB tuples outside `util.py`. Adherence test, like
  `test_no_inline_plots.py`.

## Invariants

- Figure layouts (bar arrangement, axes, reference lines, model ordering)
  must not change — only colors change.
- The report-side `fig_census_direct.pdf` (broader `census` data, ~37
  models, some without a family attribute) must still render. The
  default fallback hue covers them.
- No plot script may import the config directly; everything goes through
  `family_color()` so the config schema can evolve in one place.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `experiments/figures.toml` (or `presentation.toml`) defines exactly
      one color per family + a default fallback
- [ ] `src/aedist/util.py::family_color()` is the only function that
      reads the config
- [ ] No `src/aedist/plot_*.py` contains a hardcoded model or family
      color; all routes through `family_color()`
- [ ] Every figure that uses family colors carries an EN/FR/ZH legend
      (in-figure or via slide-side overlay)
- [ ] Unit test for `family_color()` passes
- [ ] Adherence test catches hardcoded hex/RGB in plot scripts
- [ ] `make slides/slides.pdf` and `make report/report.pdf` both build cleanly
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
